From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:49:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Enable the DSU PMU

The boot firmware for the Cubie A7S sets ACTLR_EL3 bit 12 on every core
at each reset, so the DSU PMU registers are accessible from EL2.

Enable the DSU PMU. A boot firmware without that setting must leave the
node disabled.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with firmware that grants
the access; arm_dsu_pmu probes arm_dsu_0 without an undefined
instruction.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index e50a089056e7..0d5e8cb21ccd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -130,6 +130,11 @@ &dsu {
 	dsu-supply = <&reg_dcdc5>;
 };
 
+/* the boot firmware of this board sets ACTLR_EL3 bit 12 on every core */
+&dsu_pmu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &ehci1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
